.TH SYSFORGE "1" "2026\-05\-29" "sysforge" "Generated Python Manual"
.SH NAME
sysforge
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sysforge
[-h] [-V] [-v] COMMAND ...
.SH DESCRIPTION
Arch Linux AUR helper with compiler\-optimized builds.

.SH
POSITIONAL ARGUMENTS
.TP
\fBsysforge\fR \fI\,build\/\fR
Build a package from a PKGBUILD.
.TP
\fBsysforge\fR \fI\,fetch\/\fR
Download PKGBUILD(s) into pkgbuild_src_dir without building.
.TP
\fBsysforge\fR \fI\,update\/\fR
Check for and rebuild outdated sysforge\-managed packages.
.TP
\fBsysforge\fR \fI\,resolve\/\fR
Show which profile would be applied to a package and why.
.TP
\fBsysforge\fR \fI\,converge\/\fR
Detect and repair packages whose build flags have drifted from the current profile.
.TP
\fBsysforge\fR \fI\,doctor\/\fR
Health\-check installed package depends + shared\-library linkage.
.TP
\fBsysforge\fR \fI\,packages\/\fR
Manage packages.toml override entries (list, add, remove).
.TP
\fBsysforge\fR \fI\,state\/\fR
Inspect or repair build_state.toml (live install\-state mirror).
.TP
\fBsysforge\fR \fI\,run\/\fR
Execute a pipeline stage (pipeline, hardware, reconfigure, toolchain, packages, kernel).
.TP
\fBsysforge\fR \fI\,setup\/\fR
Configure system integration (pacman IgnoreGroup for sf\-build).
.TP
\fBsysforge\fR \fI\,env\/\fR
Print the inherited env chain, all contributing sources (shell init files, systemd\-user, PAM env, sysforge [defaults] profile), and a mismatches block when sources disagree. \-vv adds inline per\-var divergence annotations.
.TP
\fBsysforge\fR \fI\,log\/\fR
Page the unified or per\-package sysforge log through $PAGER.

.SH COMMAND \fI\,'sysforge build'\/\fR
usage: sysforge build [\-h] [\-\-makepkg FLAGS] [\-\-interactive] [\-\-persist\-log]
                      [\-\-no\-pkg\-log] [\-\-log\-dir DIR] [\-\-profile\-conf FILE]
                      [\-\-cc COMPILER] [\-\-cxx COMPILER] [\-\-ld LINKER]
                      [\-\-cache\-report] [\-\-abi\-check] [\-\-no\-update]
                      [\-\-cleansrc] [\-\-cleansrc\-force] [\-\-no\-llvm\-preflight]
                      [\-\-state\-dir DIR]
                      PKGBUILD [PKGBUILD ...]

.TP
\fBPKGBUILD\fR
One or more packages to build (path, directory, or bare package name).

.SH OPTIONS \fI\,'sysforge build'\/\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-makepkg\fR \fI\,FLAGS\/\fR, \fB\-m\fR \fI\,FLAGS\/\fR
Additional makepkg flags, appended after profile makepkg_flags. Combined short
flags are expanded: \-sfci becomes \-s \-f \-c \-i. Example: sysforge build
PKGBUILD \-m '\-sfci'

.TP
\fB\-\-interactive\fR
Strip \-\-noconfirm from profile makepkg_flags and hand stdout/stderr to
makepkg's terminal so pacman conflict prompts and other unbuffered interactive
output appear immediately (disables line\-based output classification while
set).

.TP
\fB\-\-persist\-log\fR
Keep the per\-package log file after a successful build.

.TP
\fB\-\-no\-pkg\-log\fR
Disable the per\-package log file.

.TP
\fB\-\-log\-dir\fR \fI\,DIR\/\fR
Directory for the per\-package log file (default: alongside the PKGBUILD).

.TP
\fB\-\-profile\-conf\fR \fI\,FILE\/\fR
Path to a profiles.toml to use instead of the default.

.TP
\fB\-\-cc\fR \fI\,COMPILER\/\fR
Override CC (C compiler) for this build, e.g. \-\-cc clang.

.TP
\fB\-\-cxx\fR \fI\,COMPILER\/\fR
Override CXX (C++ compiler) for this build, e.g. \-\-cxx clang++.

.TP
\fB\-\-ld\fR \fI\,LINKER\/\fR
Override linker for this build, e.g. \-\-ld lld.

.TP
\fB\-\-cache\-report\fR
Print a structured cache summary (ccache/sccache hit rates) after the build.

.TP
\fB\-\-abi\-check\fR
Run a post\-build ABI compatibility check on built shared libraries.

.TP
\fB\-\-no\-update\fR
Skip git pull \-\-rebase before building.

.TP
\fB\-\-cleansrc\fR
Purge the package src dir and re\-clone before building. Refuses (per package)
if the existing clone has uncommitted changes, ahead\-of\-upstream commits, or
no upstream tracking branch.

.TP
\fB\-\-cleansrc\-force\fR
Like \-\-cleansrc but bypasses the dirty/diverged guard and overwrites the local
tree unconditionally. Use when the upstream rewrote history (e.g. Arch
packaging repos force\-push every release) and the local commits have no value
to preserve.

.TP
\fB\-\-no\-llvm\-preflight\fR
Suppress the LLVM source pre\-flight summary.

.TP
\fB\-\-state\-dir\fR \fI\,DIR\/\fR
Override state directory for build_state.toml.

.SH COMMAND \fI\,'sysforge fetch'\/\fR
usage: sysforge fetch [\-h] [\-\-no\-update] [\-\-cleansrc] [\-\-cleansrc\-force]
                      [\-\-no\-llvm\-preflight] [\-\-profile\-conf FILE]
                      PKG [PKG ...]

.TP
\fBPKG\fR
One or more package names to download.

.SH OPTIONS \fI\,'sysforge fetch'\/\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-update\fR
Skip git pull \-\-rebase for packages that are already cloned.

.TP
\fB\-\-cleansrc\fR
Purge each package's src dir and re\-clone. Refuses (per package) if the
existing clone has uncommitted changes, ahead\-of\-upstream commits, or no
upstream tracking branch.

.TP
\fB\-\-cleansrc\-force\fR
Like \-\-cleansrc but bypasses the dirty/diverged guard and overwrites the local
tree unconditionally.

.TP
\fB\-\-no\-llvm\-preflight\fR
Suppress the LLVM source pre\-flight summary.

.TP
\fB\-\-profile\-conf\fR \fI\,FILE\/\fR
Path to a profiles.toml to use instead of the default.

.SH COMMAND \fI\,'sysforge update'\/\fR
usage: sysforge update [\-h] [\-\-dry\-run] [\-\-devel] [\-\-offline] [\-\-install\-only]
                       [\-\-packages FILE] [\-\-state\-dir DIR]
                       [\-\-profile\-conf FILE] [\-\-cache\-report] [\-\-no\-pkg\-log]
                       [\-\-persist\-log] [\-\-log\-dir DIR] [\-\-makepkg FLAGS]
                       [\-\-interactive] [\-\-no\-cleanbuild] [\-\-cleansrc]
                       [\-\-cleansrc\-force] [\-\-no\-llvm\-preflight]
                       [\-\-no\-toolchain\-preflight] [\-\-include\-stage\-owned]
                       [\-\-explain\-drift] [\-\-rebuild\-on\-toolchain\-drift]
                       [PKG ...]

.TP
\fBPKG\fR
Limit update to these package names (default: all sysforge\-managed packages).

.SH OPTIONS \fI\,'sysforge update'\/\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Show what would be rebuilt without doing it.

.TP
\fB\-\-devel\fR
Resolve and rebuild VCS packages (\-git, \-svn, \-hg, \-bzr) whose upstream HEAD
has advanced past the installed version. Resolution runs makepkg \-\-nobuild per
VCS package; up\-to\-date packages are skipped, not rebuilt. Per\-package
upstream commits recorded in build_state are reused on subsequent runs to
short\-circuit the resolve via git ls\-remote.

.TP
\fB\-\-offline\fR
No network: skip git pulls, clones, and AUR RPC. Pure local version check.

.TP
\fB\-\-install\-only\fR
Skip rebuild; install only those locally\-built artifacts in PKGDEST that are
newer than the installed version. Implies \-\-offline. Mutually exclusive with
\-\-makepkg, \-\-no\-cleanbuild, \-\-cleansrc, \-\-cleansrc\-force, \-\-interactive, and
\-\-cache\-report.

.TP
\fB\-\-packages\fR \fI\,FILE\/\fR
Path to packages.toml for override rules (default:
/home/keith/src/sysforge/tests/data/etc/sysforge/packages.toml).

.TP
\fB\-\-state\-dir\fR \fI\,DIR\/\fR
Override state directory.

.TP
\fB\-\-profile\-conf\fR \fI\,FILE\/\fR
Path to a profiles.toml to use instead of the default.

.TP
\fB\-\-cache\-report\fR
Print a structured cache summary after the run.

.TP
\fB\-\-no\-pkg\-log\fR
Disable per\-package log files.

.TP
\fB\-\-persist\-log\fR
Keep log files after successful completion.

.TP
\fB\-\-log\-dir\fR \fI\,DIR\/\fR
Directory for per\-package log files.

.TP
\fB\-\-makepkg\fR \fI\,FLAGS\/\fR, \fB\-m\fR \fI\,FLAGS\/\fR
Extra flags passed verbatim to makepkg (e.g. \-m '\-f' to force rebuild).
Combined short flags are expanded: \-sfci becomes \-s \-f \-c \-i.

.TP
\fB\-\-interactive\fR
Pause on build failures to allow manual correction (default: log failure and
continue).

.TP
\fB\-\-no\-cleanbuild\fR
Skip the automatic \-\-cleanbuild (\-C) added for update runs. Useful when
packages are already built and you only need to re\-run the install step.

.TP
\fB\-\-cleansrc\fR
Purge each package's src dir and re\-clone before building. Per\-package fatal
if the clone has uncommitted changes, ahead\-of\-upstream commits, or no
upstream — that package is reported failed and the run continues.

.TP
\fB\-\-cleansrc\-force\fR
Like \-\-cleansrc but bypasses the dirty/diverged guard and overwrites every
local tree unconditionally. Use when the upstream rewrote history (e.g. Arch
packaging repos force\-push every release) and local commits have no value to
preserve.

.TP
\fB\-\-no\-llvm\-preflight\fR
Suppress the LLVM source pre\-flight summary.

.TP
\fB\-\-no\-toolchain\-preflight\fR
Skip the toolchain pre\-flight (rust/cmake/meson availability + lib32 cross
targets) that normally runs before the build loop.

.TP
\fB\-\-include\-stage\-owned\fR
Include packages owned by a pipeline stage (e.g. the kernel stage's `linux\-
custom`). Skipped by default; the owning stage (`sysforge run kernel`) is the
canonical update path.

.TP
\fB\-\-explain\-drift\fR
List packages whose recorded toolchain_variant differs from the currently
active toolchain (gcc / stock_llvm / pgo_llvm) and exit. Informational; no
source sync, no rebuild.

.TP
\fB\-\-rebuild\-on\-toolchain\-drift\fR
Treat toolchain\-variant drift as an upgrade trigger: packages built under a
different toolchain than is active now are added to the rebuild queue. Off by
default — drift is reported but not acted on, since most C/C++ packages don't
measurably benefit from a re\-stamp.

.SH COMMAND \fI\,'sysforge resolve'\/\fR
usage: sysforge resolve [\-h] [\-\-show\-flags | \-\-deps] [\-\-profile\-conf FILE] PKG

.TP
\fBPKG\fR
Path to a PKGBUILD file, or bare package name.

.SH OPTIONS \fI\,'sysforge resolve'\/\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-show\-flags\fR
Print the full resolved flag set.

.TP
\fB\-\-deps\fR
Show transitive dependency tree with build order instead of profile info.

.TP
\fB\-\-profile\-conf\fR \fI\,FILE\/\fR
Path to a profiles.toml to use instead of the default.

.SH COMMAND \fI\,'sysforge converge'\/\fR
usage: sysforge converge [\-h] [\-\-apply] [\-\-state\-dir DIR]
                         [\-\-profile\-conf FILE] [\-\-no\-pkg\-log] [\-\-persist\-log]
                         [\-\-log\-dir DIR] [\-\-makepkg FLAGS] [\-\-cache\-report]
                         [\-\-no\-llvm\-preflight]
                         [PKG ...]

.TP
\fBPKG\fR
Limit drift check to these package names (default: all build_state\-recorded
packages).

.SH OPTIONS \fI\,'sysforge converge'\/\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-apply\fR
Rebuild all DRIFTED packages with the current profile.

.TP
\fB\-\-state\-dir\fR \fI\,DIR\/\fR
Override state directory for build_state.toml.

.TP
\fB\-\-profile\-conf\fR \fI\,FILE\/\fR
Path to a profiles.toml to use instead of the default.

.TP
\fB\-\-no\-pkg\-log\fR
Disable per\-package log files (only relevant with \-\-apply).

.TP
\fB\-\-persist\-log\fR
Keep log files after successful completion (only relevant with \-\-apply).

.TP
\fB\-\-log\-dir\fR \fI\,DIR\/\fR
Directory for per\-package log files (only relevant with \-\-apply).

.TP
\fB\-\-makepkg\fR \fI\,FLAGS\/\fR, \fB\-m\fR \fI\,FLAGS\/\fR
Extra flags passed to makepkg during \-\-apply rebuilds (e.g. \-m '\-C' to
cleanbuild). \-f is always injected automatically.

.TP
\fB\-\-cache\-report\fR
Print a structured cache summary after \-\-apply runs.

.TP
\fB\-\-no\-llvm\-preflight\fR
Suppress the LLVM source pre\-flight summary.

.SH COMMAND \fI\,'sysforge doctor'\/\fR
usage: sysforge doctor [\-h] [\-\-graphics] [\-\-all] [\-\-repo] [\-\-shallow]
                       [\-\-quiet] [\-\-suggest] [\-\-apply] [\-\-no\-confirm]
                       [\-\-dry\-run]
                       [PKG ...]

.TP
\fBPKG\fR
One or more installed package names to verify. Without any
PKG/\-\-graphics/\-\-all, the command exits with usage.

.SH OPTIONS \fI\,'sysforge doctor'\/\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-graphics\fR
Expand to the graphics stack (mesa, vulkan, libglvnd, wayland, libdrm, libva,
libvdpau, egl\-wayland, xwayland, gamescope, plus per\-vendor drivers from the
hardware overlay's gpu_vendors) AND run system\-state probes (nvidia\-drm
modeset, driver version skew, Wayland explicit\-sync protocol, Steam GPU accel,
session type).

.TP
\fB\-\-all\fR
Verify every installed package — foreign and non\-foreign (pacman \-Q). Slow but
comprehensive.

.TP
\fB\-\-repo\fR
Verify every non\-foreign (native repo) package. Narrower than \-\-all.

.TP
\fB\-\-shallow\fR
Do not recurse into transitive dependencies of each target.

.TP
\fB\-\-quiet\fR, \fB\-q\fR
Suppress clean lines; print only packages with issues.

.TP
\fB\-\-suggest\fR, \fB\-s\fR
For each unsatisfied soname, look up candidate packages via `pacman \-Fq`.
Findings split into 'install candidates' (missing from disk — install the
package), 'rebuild candidates' (installed; rebuild against the current
system), and 'ABI\-drift candidates' (present but one of their versioned
symbols no longer resolves — rebuild or upgrade, not reinstall). Requires a
synced files db (`sudo pacman \-Fy`).

.TP
\fB\-\-apply\fR
Hand the rebuild candidates from \-\-suggest off to `sysforge update` and
rebuild them. Implies \-\-suggest. Drift\-rebuild only in v1.x — install
candidates are printed but not invoked.

.TP
\fB\-\-no\-confirm\fR
Skip the y/N prompt before \-\-apply rebuilds.

.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Report what \-\-apply would rebuild without invoking the build.

.SH COMMAND \fI\,'sysforge packages'\/\fR
usage: sysforge packages [\-h] [\-\-packages FILE] [\-\-orphans]
                         {list,add,remove} ...

.SH
POSITIONAL ARGUMENTS \fI\,'sysforge packages'\/\fR
.TP
\fBsysforge packages\fR \fI\,list\/\fR
Show override entries in packages.toml.
.TP
\fBsysforge packages\fR \fI\,add\/\fR
Add or update an override entry. Requires at least one of \-\-pkgbuild\-patch / \-\-no\-cache / \-\-reason.
.TP
\fBsysforge packages\fR \fI\,remove\/\fR
Remove an override entry.

.SH COMMAND \fI\,'sysforge packages list'\/\fR
usage: sysforge packages list [\-h] [\-\-packages FILE] [\-\-orphans]

.SH OPTIONS \fI\,'sysforge packages list'\/\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-packages\fR \fI\,FILE\/\fR
Path to packages.toml.

.TP
\fB\-\-orphans\fR
Show only entries whose package is not currently installed.

.SH COMMAND \fI\,'sysforge packages add'\/\fR
usage: sysforge packages add [\-h] [\-\-source {repo,aur,local}]
                             [\-\-pkgbuild\-patch] [\-\-no\-cache] [\-\-reason TEXT]
                             [\-\-packages FILE]
                             PKG

.TP
\fBPKG\fR
Package name to add or update.

.SH OPTIONS \fI\,'sysforge packages add'\/\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-source\fR \fI\,{repo,aur,local}\/\fR
Pin routing (metadata; doesn't satisfy validation on its own). `local` marks a
hand\-maintained PKGBUILD with no remote to sync from.

.TP
\fB\-\-pkgbuild\-patch\fR
Patch PKGBUILD flags before build.

.TP
\fB\-\-no\-cache\fR
Disable ccache/sccache for this package (required for PGO).

.TP
\fB\-\-reason\fR \fI\,TEXT\/\fR
Free\-form note attached to the entry.

.TP
\fB\-\-packages\fR \fI\,FILE\/\fR
Path to packages.toml.

.SH COMMAND \fI\,'sysforge packages remove'\/\fR
usage: sysforge packages remove [\-h] [\-\-packages FILE] PKG

.TP
\fBPKG\fR
Package name to remove.

.SH OPTIONS \fI\,'sysforge packages remove'\/\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-packages\fR \fI\,FILE\/\fR
Path to packages.toml.

.SH OPTIONS \fI\,'sysforge packages'\/\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-packages\fR \fI\,FILE\/\fR
Path to packages.toml (default:
/home/keith/src/sysforge/tests/data/etc/sysforge/packages.toml).

.TP
\fB\-\-orphans\fR
With list: show only entries whose package is not currently installed.

.SH COMMAND \fI\,'sysforge state'\/\fR
usage: sysforge state [\-h] {list,repair,orphans,failed} ...

.SH
POSITIONAL ARGUMENTS \fI\,'sysforge state'\/\fR
.TP
\fBsysforge state\fR \fI\,list\/\fR
Tabulate build_state.toml entries.
.TP
\fBsysforge state\fR \fI\,repair\/\fR
Re\-parse PKGBUILDs to rewrite build_state.toml entries that contain unexpanded shell variables (e.g. '$_pkgname\-git').
.TP
\fBsysforge state\fR \fI\,orphans\/\fR
List (and optionally prune) stale .pkg.tar* artifacts in PKGDEST. Only surfaces superseded files (pkgname installed AND artifact older than installed) so \-\-prune is always safe.
.TP
\fBsysforge state\fR \fI\,failed\/\fR
List packages whose last build failed (recorded in build_state.toml), with any diagnosed fix. Entries auto\-clear on the next successful build.

.SH COMMAND \fI\,'sysforge state list'\/\fR
usage: sysforge state list [\-h] [\-\-state\-dir DIR] [\-\-no\-pager]

.SH OPTIONS \fI\,'sysforge state list'\/\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-state\-dir\fR \fI\,DIR\/\fR
Override state directory.

.TP
\fB\-\-no\-pager\fR
Don't pipe output through $PAGER (default: paginate when stdout is a TTY).

.SH COMMAND \fI\,'sysforge state repair'\/\fR
usage: sysforge state repair [\-h] [\-\-state\-dir DIR] [\-\-dry\-run]

.SH OPTIONS \fI\,'sysforge state repair'\/\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-state\-dir\fR \fI\,DIR\/\fR
Override state directory.

.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Show the planned repair without writing.

.SH COMMAND \fI\,'sysforge state orphans'\/\fR
usage: sysforge state orphans [\-h] [\-\-prune] [\-\-no\-confirm] [\-\-no\-pager]

.SH OPTIONS \fI\,'sysforge state orphans'\/\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-prune\fR
Delete the listed superseded artifacts (prompts for confirmation).

.TP
\fB\-\-no\-confirm\fR
Skip the y/N prompt when pruning. Implies \-\-prune.

.TP
\fB\-\-no\-pager\fR
Don't pipe output through $PAGER (default: paginate when stdout is a TTY).

.SH COMMAND \fI\,'sysforge state failed'\/\fR
usage: sysforge state failed [\-h] [\-\-state\-dir DIR] [\-\-no\-pager]
                             [\-\-clear PKGBASE] [\-\-clear\-all]

.SH OPTIONS \fI\,'sysforge state failed'\/\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-state\-dir\fR \fI\,DIR\/\fR
Override state directory.

.TP
\fB\-\-no\-pager\fR
Don't pipe output through $PAGER (default: paginate when stdout is a TTY).

.TP
\fB\-\-clear\fR \fI\,PKGBASE\/\fR
Clear the recorded failure for PKGBASE and exit.

.TP
\fB\-\-clear\-all\fR
Clear all recorded failures and exit.

.SH COMMAND \fI\,'sysforge run'\/\fR
usage: sysforge run [\-h] STAGE ...

.SH
POSITIONAL ARGUMENTS \fI\,'sysforge run'\/\fR
.TP
\fBsysforge run\fR \fI\,pipeline\/\fR
Run the full install pipeline (stages 1–8).
.TP
\fBsysforge run\fR \fI\,hardware\/\fR
Re\-run hardware detection and refresh hardware_profile.toml.
.TP
\fBsysforge run\fR \fI\,reconfigure\/\fR
Pre\-build checkpoint: review configs, disk, network, GPG, build preview.
.TP
\fBsysforge run\fR \fI\,toolchain\/\fR
Build and install the LLVM/GCC toolchain from toolchain.toml.
.TP
\fBsysforge run\fR \fI\,packages\/\fR
Build and install non\-kernel packages from packages.toml.
.TP
\fBsysforge run\fR \fI\,kernel\/\fR
Build and install the custom kernel configured in kernel.toml.

.SH COMMAND \fI\,'sysforge run pipeline'\/\fR
usage: sysforge run pipeline [\-h] [\-\-resume] [\-\-start\-from STAGE]
                             [\-\-force\-retry] [\-\-dry\-run] [\-\-packages FILE]
                             [\-\-state\-dir DIR] [\-\-no\-unified\-log]
                             [\-\-no\-pkg\-logs] [\-\-log\-dir DIR] [\-\-purge\-log]
                             [\-\-persist\-log] [\-\-profile\-conf FILE]
                             [\-\-cache\-report] [\-\-abi\-check] [\-\-no\-update]

.SH OPTIONS \fI\,'sysforge run pipeline'\/\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-resume\fR
Resume from the last checkpoint.

.TP
\fB\-\-start\-from\fR \fI\,STAGE\/\fR
Start from this stage, marking all prior stages as skipped. Useful on a live
system: \-\-start\-from reconfigure

.TP
\fB\-\-force\-retry\fR
Retry all failed packages without prompting.

.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Show what would run without executing anything.

.TP
\fB\-\-packages\fR \fI\,FILE\/\fR
Path to packages.toml (default:
/home/keith/src/sysforge/tests/data/etc/sysforge/packages.toml).

.TP
\fB\-\-state\-dir\fR \fI\,DIR\/\fR
Override state directory.

.TP
\fB\-\-no\-unified\-log\fR
Disable the unified log file.

.TP
\fB\-\-no\-pkg\-logs\fR
Disable per\-package log files.

.TP
\fB\-\-log\-dir\fR \fI\,DIR\/\fR
Directory for log files.

.TP
\fB\-\-purge\-log\fR
Truncate the unified log before this run.

.TP
\fB\-\-persist\-log\fR
Keep log files after successful completion.

.TP
\fB\-\-profile\-conf\fR \fI\,FILE\/\fR
Path to a profiles.toml to use instead of the default.

.TP
\fB\-\-cache\-report\fR
Print a structured cache summary after the pipeline completes.

.TP
\fB\-\-abi\-check\fR
Run a post\-build ABI compatibility check on built shared libraries.

.TP
\fB\-\-no\-update\fR
Skip git pull \-\-rebase before each build.

.SH COMMAND \fI\,'sysforge run hardware'\/\fR
usage: sysforge run hardware [\-h] [\-\-dry\-run] [\-\-state\-dir DIR]

.SH OPTIONS \fI\,'sysforge run hardware'\/\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Show what would be written without writing.

.TP
\fB\-\-state\-dir\fR \fI\,DIR\/\fR
Override state directory.

.SH COMMAND \fI\,'sysforge run reconfigure'\/\fR
usage: sysforge run reconfigure [\-h] [\-\-dry\-run] [\-\-packages FILE]
                                [\-\-state\-dir DIR]

.SH OPTIONS \fI\,'sysforge run reconfigure'\/\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Run all steps non\-interactively without writing any changes.

.TP
\fB\-\-packages\fR \fI\,FILE\/\fR
Path to packages.toml (used by disk and preview steps).

.TP
\fB\-\-state\-dir\fR \fI\,DIR\/\fR
Override state directory.

.SH COMMAND \fI\,'sysforge run toolchain'\/\fR
usage: sysforge run toolchain [\-h] [\-\-dry\-run] [\-\-no\-update] [\-\-makepkg FLAGS]
                              [\-\-persist\-log] [\-\-cache\-report] [\-\-abi\-check]
                              [\-\-state\-dir DIR] [\-\-rebuild\-profdata]
                              [\-\-auto\-pgo] [\-\-allow\-dirty\-llvm] [\-\-cleansrc]
                              [\-\-cleansrc\-force]

.SH OPTIONS \fI\,'sysforge run toolchain'\/\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Show what would run without executing anything.

.TP
\fB\-\-no\-update\fR
Skip git pull \-\-rebase before each build.

.TP
\fB\-\-makepkg\fR \fI\,FLAGS\/\fR, \fB\-m\fR \fI\,FLAGS\/\fR
Additional makepkg flags appended to each build. Example: \-m '\-f' to force
rebuild of already\-built packages. Install flags (\-i/\-\-install) are ignored;
the toolchain controls which passes install to the system.

.TP
\fB\-\-persist\-log\fR
Keep log files after successful completion.

.TP
\fB\-\-cache\-report\fR
Print a structured cache summary after the run.

.TP
\fB\-\-abi\-check\fR
Run a post\-build ABI compatibility check on built shared libraries.

.TP
\fB\-\-state\-dir\fR \fI\,DIR\/\fR
Override state directory.

.TP
\fB\-\-rebuild\-profdata\fR
Force a full 4\-pass PGO build even if compatible profdata already exists.

.TP
\fB\-\-auto\-pgo\fR
Bypass the PGO confirmation prompts (profdata reuse, staging/pgo_store purge,
4\-pass start, suspicious profdata size). Required for non\-interactive PGO
runs; without it, a non\-TTY invocation aborts the PGO sub\-flow because PGO is
fragile and silent mis\-optimisation is the failure mode.

.TP
\fB\-\-allow\-dirty\-llvm\fR
Bypass the LLVM safety pre\-flight refusal on dirty or diverged trees. PGO
profdata version mismatches cannot be bypassed. Note: this only suppresses the
refusal — it does not modify the tree. Use \-\-cleansrc\-force to actually
overwrite the local trees with upstream.

.TP
\fB\-\-cleansrc\fR
Purge each toolchain package's src dir and re\-clone before building. Refuses
(per package) if the existing clone has uncommitted changes, ahead\-of\-upstream
commits, or no upstream.

.TP
\fB\-\-cleansrc\-force\fR
Like \-\-cleansrc but bypasses the dirty/diverged guard and overwrites every
local toolchain tree unconditionally. Use when the upstream rewrote history
(e.g. Arch packaging repos force\-push every release) and local commits have no
value.

.SH COMMAND \fI\,'sysforge run packages'\/\fR
usage: sysforge run packages [\-h] [\-\-packages FILE] [\-\-dry\-run]
                             [\-\-force\-retry] [\-\-no\-update] [\-\-no\-pkg\-logs]
                             [\-\-persist\-log] [\-\-log\-dir DIR] [\-\-cache\-report]
                             [\-\-abi\-check] [\-\-state\-dir DIR]
                             [\-\-profile\-conf FILE]

.SH OPTIONS \fI\,'sysforge run packages'\/\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-packages\fR \fI\,FILE\/\fR
Path to packages.toml (default:
/home/keith/src/sysforge/tests/data/etc/sysforge/packages.toml).

.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Show what would run without executing anything.

.TP
\fB\-\-force\-retry\fR
Retry all failed packages without prompting.

.TP
\fB\-\-no\-update\fR
Skip git pull \-\-rebase before each build.

.TP
\fB\-\-no\-pkg\-logs\fR
Disable per\-package log files.

.TP
\fB\-\-persist\-log\fR
Keep log files after successful completion.

.TP
\fB\-\-log\-dir\fR \fI\,DIR\/\fR
Directory for log files.

.TP
\fB\-\-cache\-report\fR
Print a structured cache summary after the run.

.TP
\fB\-\-abi\-check\fR
Run a post\-build ABI compatibility check on built shared libraries.

.TP
\fB\-\-state\-dir\fR \fI\,DIR\/\fR
Override state directory.

.TP
\fB\-\-profile\-conf\fR \fI\,FILE\/\fR
Path to a profiles.toml to use instead of the default.

.SH COMMAND \fI\,'sysforge run kernel'\/\fR
usage: sysforge run kernel [\-h] [\-\-dry\-run] [\-\-no\-update] [\-\-cleansrc]
                           [\-\-cleansrc\-force] [\-\-non\-interactive]
                           [\-\-compiler {gcc,llvm}]
                           [\-\-bootloader {systemd\-boot,grub,none}]
                           [\-\-no\-pkg\-logs] [\-\-persist\-log] [\-\-log\-dir DIR]
                           [\-\-cache\-report] [\-\-abi\-check] [\-\-state\-dir DIR]
                           [\-\-profile\-conf FILE]

.SH OPTIONS \fI\,'sysforge run kernel'\/\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Show what would run without executing anything.

.TP
\fB\-\-no\-update\fR
Skip git pull \-\-rebase before each build.

.TP
\fB\-\-cleansrc\fR
Purge the kernel src dir and re\-clone before building. Refuses if the existing
clone has uncommitted changes, ahead\-of\-upstream commits, or no upstream.

.TP
\fB\-\-cleansrc\-force\fR
Like \-\-cleansrc but bypasses the dirty/diverged guard and overwrites the local
tree unconditionally.

.TP
\fB\-\-non\-interactive\fR
Disable interactive kconfig (default is interactive — the PKGBUILD's `make
nconfig`/`menuconfig`/etc. runs as written). With this flag, interactive
targets are patched to `make olddefconfig` for unattended runs.

.TP
\fB\-\-compiler\fR \fI\,{gcc,llvm}\/\fR
Kernel\-stage compiler override (gcc or llvm). Independent of the global
toolchain stage — lets you keep gcc system\-wide but build the kernel with LLVM
(or vice versa). Resolution order: this flag > kernel.toml compiler >
toolchain\-stage pipeline state.

.TP
\fB\-\-bootloader\fR \fI\,{systemd\-boot,grub,none}\/\fR
Override kernel.toml bootloader for this invocation (systemd\-boot is the
default).

.TP
\fB\-\-no\-pkg\-logs\fR
Disable per\-package log files.

.TP
\fB\-\-persist\-log\fR
Keep log files after successful completion.

.TP
\fB\-\-log\-dir\fR \fI\,DIR\/\fR
Directory for log files.

.TP
\fB\-\-cache\-report\fR
Print a structured cache summary after the run.

.TP
\fB\-\-abi\-check\fR
Run a post\-build ABI compatibility check on built shared libraries.

.TP
\fB\-\-state\-dir\fR \fI\,DIR\/\fR
Override state directory.

.TP
\fB\-\-profile\-conf\fR \fI\,FILE\/\fR
Path to a profiles.toml to use instead of the default.

.SH COMMAND \fI\,'sysforge setup'\/\fR
usage: sysforge setup [\-h] [\-\-pacman\-conf FILE]

.SH OPTIONS \fI\,'sysforge setup'\/\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-pacman\-conf\fR \fI\,FILE\/\fR
Path to pacman.conf (default: /etc/pacman.conf).

.SH COMMAND \fI\,'sysforge env'\/\fR
usage: sysforge env [\-h]

.SH COMMAND \fI\,'sysforge log'\/\fR
usage: sysforge log [\-h] [\-\-state\-dir DIR] [\-\-no\-pager] [PKG]

.TP
\fBPKG\fR
Package name (resolves to <pkgbuild_src_dir>/<pkg>/sysforge_<pkg>.log). Omit
to page the unified log.

.SH OPTIONS \fI\,'sysforge log'\/\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-state\-dir\fR \fI\,DIR\/\fR
Override state directory (used to locate the unified log).

.TP
\fB\-\-no\-pager\fR
Don't pipe output through $PAGER (default: paginate when stdout is a TTY).

.SH COMMAND \fI\,'sysforge completions'\/\fR
usage: sysforge completions [\-h] {packages,manifest,local,state,makepkg\-flags}

.TP
\fB{packages,manifest,local,state,makepkg\-flags}\fR

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
show program's version number and exit

.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Verbosity level. Default: errors only. \-v adds warnings. \-vv adds
informational messages. \-vvv adds debug output.

